d by different individuals. These items can neither be simply placed on the 'orderable' list because someone dislikes them nor on the 'not_orderable' list because someone likes them.\n\nConflicted Foods: tacos, caramel, pie, salmon, nachos, espresso, spaghetti, tiramisu, pho.\n\nSince each of these items is liked by at least one person and disliked by another, we'll need to be more strategic in determining their placement or exclusion from the orderable lists. Let's start by fulfilling the needs of individuals with unique preferences that do not conflict with others:\n\n1. Rohan, Yue, Ava, Om, Pam like pie and it's not disliked by anyone else so we can safely add it to 'orderable.' Arun does dislike pie, but pie must be included to satisfy the others who like it. Therefore, for Arun to be satisfied, a food that he dislikes must be 'not_orderable'.\n2. Du and Min like tiramisu and it's only disliked by Abe. So, for Abe to be satisfied, a food he dislikes must be 'not_orderable'.\n3. Du, Min, Gen, and Zoe all dislike espresso and no one has it on their like list, so it can be placed on the 'not_orderable' list.\n\nUpdating the lists based on these initial considerations:\n\norderable: pie\nnot_orderable: espresso\n\nNow, remaining conflicted foods: tacos, caramel, salmon, nachos, spaghetti, pho, and tiramisu. We need to satisfy the following individuals with their unique dislikes:\n- Arun dislikes tacos, nachos, and pie is already orderable, so he is satisfied.\n- Xan dislikes pho, salmon, and tacos, since tacos haven't been placed yet, we can still satisfy Xan.\n\nConsidering that Arun is already satisfied by pie being orderable, we can now place one of Xan's disliked foods on the 'not_orderable' list. Pho is only liked by Ken and Cal, but Cal has another like (salmon) which isn't on the not_orderable list yet, making pho the better choice for 'not_orderable' to satisfy both Ken and Xan.\n\nUpdating the lists:\n\norderable: pie\nnot_orderable: espresso, pho\n\nThis would satisfy Ken (since he dislikes pho and likes nachos, which is not on either list yet). Cal will be satisfied with salmon, which we haven't placed yet.\n\nContinuing with other conflicted foods:\n- Caramel is liked by Taj, Pia, Hui, Wei, Jay, Abe, and Min but disliked by Ava and Om. Since Ava likes pie and Om dislikes caramel, to satisfy Om we need to ensure a food Om dislikes is not_orderable. Om also dislikes spaghetti, which is only liked by Ken who is already satisfied by nachos not being on either list. We will put spaghetti on the 'not_orderable' list.\n\norderable: pie\nnot_orderable: espresso, pho, spaghetti\n\nThis would satisfy Om as well. With the current lists, everyone who dislikes caramel (Ava and Om) are already satisfied because food they dislike (spaghetti) is on the 'not_orderable' list.\n\nAva is also satisfied with pie. Thus, caramel can safely be added to the 'orderable' list.\n\norderable: pie, caramel\nnot_orderable: espresso, pho, spaghetti\n\nLet's reassess the remaining conflicted foods: tacos, salmon, nachos, tiramisu.\n- Tacos are liked by Taj but disliked by many. To satisfy those who dislike tacos, they must remain off the 'orderable' list.\n- Salmon is liked by Pia, Zara, Jay, Cal, and disliked by Wei and Xan. Since Xan and Wei are both not yet satisfied and dislike salmon, it will remain off the 'orderable' list for now.\n- Nachos are liked by Zara, Ken, and Pam but disliked by Arun. Arun is already satisfied with pie so nachos can be orderable.\n- Tiramisu is liked by Du, Min, Gen, and Zoe, but disliked by Abe and Cal. Abe is already satisfied with caramel (his like) being orderable. Cal is satisfied with pie being orderable, which allows us to place tiramisu on the 'orderable' list.\n\nUpdating the lists, we have:\n\norderable: pie, caramel, nachos, tiramisu\nnot_orderable: espresso, pho, spaghetti\n\nEveryone who dislikes tacos, salmon, and the items on our not_orderable list are now satisfied because those items are not on the