n \'not_orderable\' because it\'s liked by Mei, Diya, Jaya.\n- Baklava should be on \'orderable\' because Lei likes it; no one with a dislike for baklava has no other alternatives satisfied from \'orderable\'.\n- Couscous is liked by several people, but no one with a dislike for couscous lacks other alternatives satisfied from \'orderable\'.\n  \nNow let\'s see if all individuals can be satisfied under the current "orderable" list of tacos, vegetables, churros, and baklava.\n\nStep 5: Check individuals not directly addressed yet:\n- Ru dislikes tiramisu, couscous, and vegetables, but is satisfied due to vegetables being \'orderable\'.\n- Xan dislikes roti, baklava, couscous, but is satisfied due to baklava being \'orderable\'.\n- Shan likes tiramisu, is not satisfied, so tiramisu must be added to \'orderable\'.\n- Diya dislikes vegetables, but likes macaron and shawarma, which aren\'t on any list yet.\n- Min dislikes baklava but likes couscous and tacos, and is satisfied due to tacos being \'orderable\'.\n- Rob dislikes tacos and baklava but likes vegetables; he\'s satisfied due to vegetables being \'orderable\'.\n- Liv dislikes frittata, tacos, shawarma, is satisfied due to tacos being \'orderable\'.\n- Lex likes tacos and frittata; he\'s satisfied with tacos being \'orderable\'.\n- Du likes shawarma but dislikes macaron and churros; shawarma must be added to \'orderable\'.\n- Oli likes shawarma but dislikes roti and couscous, will be satisfied with shawarma \'orderable\'.\n- Geet likes couscous, roti, and dislikes baklava; no conflicts so Geet is satisfied with existing \'orderable\'.\n- Jon likes roti, vegetables, dislikes macaron; satisfied due to vegetables being \'orderable\'.\n- Ana likes tiramisu, tacos, dislikes roti; satisfied with shawarma and tiramisu \'orderable\'.\n\nStep 6: Resolve remaining conflicts\n- Diya dislikes vegetables but likes macaron and shawarma, and with now shawarma being \'orderable\' she\'s satisfied.\n\nBy adding tiramisu and shawarma to \'orderable\', all persons are satisfied based on the given criteria.\n\nFinally, here\'s the solution with no conflict:\n```\norderable=[\'tacos\', \'vegetables\', \'churros\', \'baklava\', \'tiramisu\', \'shawarma\'], not_orderable=[]\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 483, 'num_completion_tokens': 1210}
