, Lex, Taj, Ying, Lei. Salad is a difficult case as a lot of people both like and dislike it.\n\n- Nachos are liked by Hu, Ada, Amy, but disliked by Bo, Lex, Rohan, Mia, Fay, Ana, Lei. It appears more people dislike nachos than like them.\n\n- Waffles is liked by Hu, but disliked by Leo, Xan, Fay, Ana, Mia, Amy. It is disliked more often than liked.\n\nBased on this, let's tentatively assign items to each list and then verify if all individuals' preferences are met:\n\nOrderable: burrito, guacamole, tacos, bruschetta\nNot_orderable: salmon, doughnut, nachos, waffles, salad\n\n2. Adjust based on satisfaction criteria:\n\nIf an individual's liked item is in the 'orderable' list or their disliked item is in the 'not_orderable' list, they are satisfied. We will now iterate through every individual to check whether they are satisfied with the current list.\n\nHu: Nachos are not_orderable, satisfied.\nAbe: Salmon is not_orderable, satisfied.\nCy: Doughnut is not_orderable, satisfied.\nHal: Salmon is not_orderable, satisfied.\nVic: Tacos are orderable, satisfied.\nAnil: Guacamole is orderable, so Anil is not satisfied, adjust bruschetta to not_orderable.\nBo: Guacamole is orderable, satisfied.\nKit: Doughnut is not_orderable, satisfied.\nAda: Nachos are not_orderable, satisfied.\nTim: Salad is not_orderable, satisfied.\nRu: Doughnut is not_orderable, satisfied.\nJoy: Doughnut and salmon are not_orderable, satisfied.\nGia: Guacamole is orderable, satisfied.\nRavi: Guacamole is not_orderable, satisfied.\nRina: Tacos are orderable, satisfied.\nZac: Salad is not_orderable, satisfied.\nLex: Salad and salmon are not_orderable, satisfied.\nSam: Bruschetta is not_orderable, satisfied.\nXiu: Salad is not_orderable, satisfied.\nOli: Bruschetta is not_orderable, satisfied.\nRohan: Guacamole is orderable, dissatisfied. Guacamole should be not_orderable.\nJay: Salmon is not_orderable, satisfied.\nFay: Tacos are orderable, satisfied.\nMax: Salad is not_orderable, satisfied.\nSol: Salmon