iked by others (Rex, Diya, Gen, Hal, Joy, Oli, Eli, Nic), thus it’s also contentious.\n\nWe can’t immediately find any food item that is unanimously liked or disliked. Now let\'s try to find items that can satisfy those with likes that don\'t conflict with many dislikes.\n\nFrom the above analysis, lasagna could potentially be put in the \'not_orderable\' list since it\'s disliked by many and only a few people like it. By placing lasagna in the \'not_orderable\' list, we satisfy those who dislike it.\n\nNow, considering individual requirements:\n- Anyone who likes lasagna and doesn\'t have any other likes cannot be satisfied because lasagna is potentially \'not_orderable\'.\n- Anyone disliking a food other than lasagna may get their satisfaction from the \'not_orderable\' list if the disliked item is unique to them or collectively disliked.\n\nNext, we must pick items for the \'orderable\' list, ensuring that we do not include any item that is disliked by someone we are trying to satisfy with lasagna being \'not_orderable.\'\n\nSince waffles are liked by almost everyone and only disliked by a few who also dislike lasagna (except for Joe who dislikes cheesecake as well but likes caramel), let\'s try to place "waffles" in the \'orderable\' list. This would satisfy numerous people.\n\nBy placing lasagna in \'not_orderable\' and waffles in \'orderable\', we satisfy many people:\n\n- Tara is not satisfied yet because baklava and caramel are neither orderable nor not_orderable.\n- Abe gets waffles and lasagna is not available, therefore is satisfied.\n- Rex is satisfied because baklava is not \'orderable\'.\n- Liz gets waffles, so is satisfied.\n- Lan is satisfied with waffles and no lasagna.\n- Ian is satisfied with waffles and no lasagna.\n- Lex gets both caramel and cheesecake.\n- Hal is satisfied by the absence of lasagna and cheesecake.\n- Bea is satisfied with waffles and no lasagna.\n- Diya is satisfied with waffles and no baklava or caramel.\n- Mel is satisfied with waffles.\n- Sam is not satisfied yet because baklava is still pending.\n- Isha is satisfied with caramel.\n- Pia is not satisfied yet because baklava is pending.\n- Bao is satisfied with waffles and no lasagna or caramel.\n- Gen is satisfied with waffles and no lasagna or baklava.\n- Bo is satisfied with waffles and no lasagna.\n- Ula is satisfied by no waffles or cheesecake.\n- Ivy is satisfied with caramel.\n- Amy is satisfied with waffles and no lasagna or caramel.\n- Ru is not satisfied because lasagna and cheesecake are not in the \'orderable\' list and caramel in the \'orderable\' is not enough.\n- Eli is satisfied by no baklava or caramel.\n- Jaya is satisfied with caramel.\n- Joe is only satisfied with caramel. (Joe dislikes cheesecake, but we can\'t exclude it from the \'orderable\' list without more information)\n- Neil is satisfied with waffles and no baklava or cheesecake.\n- Sky is not satisfied yet because baklava and cheesecake are still pending.\n- Sal is satisfied with waffles.\n- Ada is satisfied with caramel.\n- Geet is satisfied by no baklava or caramel.\n- Qi is satisfied by no waffles or cheesecake.\n- Sol is not satisfied yet because baklava and cheesecake are still pending.\n- Jun is satisfied with caramel.\n- Oli is satisfied by no caramel or baklava.\n- Nic is satisfied by no caramel.\n- Mia is satisfied by no lasagna or cheesecake.\n- Ray is satisfied with caramel.\n- Li is satisfied with cheesecake and no caramel or lasagna.\n- Joy dislike everything, and there\'s nothing exclusively in the \'orderable\' that Joy dislikes, so Joy is potentially a problem.\n- Tao is not satisfied yet because baklava is pending.\n- Ron is satisfied with caramel and no waffles.\n\nThe remaining people are Tara, Sam, Pia, Ru, Sky, Sol, Tao, Joy. Among them:\n\n- Joy cannot be satisfied because they dislike everything, and there\'s nothing in \'orderable\' that they dislike.\n- Sam, Pia, Tara, Tao, Sky, Sol like baklava which is not yet in any list. By putting baklava in \'orderable\' we can satisfy them.\n- Ru also likes lasagna and dislikes cheesecake, but with caramel in \'orderable\', Ru would be satisfied.\n\nHowever, since we cannot satisfy Joy (who dislikes everything available and does not have a unique like), we have to conclude that it\'s impossible to come up with a selection that will satisfy everyone. Therefore, according to the given rules, both lists should be empty:\n\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 737, 'num_completion_tokens': 1451}
